Subject: [PATCH] fix(provider): bound a persistent logins.json read failure's
 log (#7008)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed: sharedLogins logged its read failure on every ask, and
filememo retries an unreadable file on every read, so an owner change
making every read fail wrote ~500 identical lines a second — 14.7M lines,
2.2 GB in 8 hours (#7008), then the disk. The first failure of a run is
logged at once, the same error later once per 5 minutes with how many
went by quiet in between, and a read that succeeds (or finds the file
gone, or recovers the last good generation) logs a new failure at once.
A different error is never held back. The kept-accounts semantics are
unchanged: lastLogins is still served and kept, as
TestLoginsKeptWhileAnotherMagpieWrites covers, and the .bak/.bad-
recovery is untouched. providers-accounts.md notes the bounded log.

Run: TestUnreadLoginsLogRateBounded (new) fails on base 1e2287758 with
25 lines from 25 reads and passes with the fix; product-only ablation
red, restored green. Targeted -race (unread/kept family) passes. gofmt
and git diff --check clean; vet darwin/linux/windows and builds
darwin/windows/linux pass. `go test -tags nogui -timeout=45m
-count=1 ./internal/provider/` exits 1 with TestResolveVia alone, the
documented local proxy-isolation failure: the same failure on bare base
1e2287758 and with the new test skipped. (An earlier package run hit a
TestHandOver panic that did not reproduce in three later runs, two with
the new test present.)

